public:
    void sendPacket(Packet& packet); // Send a packet to a network
    Packet receivePacket(); // Receive a packet from a network
    bool checkRoutingPacket(Packet& packet); // Check the validity of a routing packet

private:
    bool addPacketToRoute(Packet, Router*);
    Packet findMatchingPacket(Packet& packet);
    bool packetMatches(Packet& packet, const Route&);
};
```

The `sendPacket` and `receivePacket` methods expose the core functionality, while `addPacketToRoute`, `findMatchingPacket`, and `packetMatches` are hidden.

### Transport Layer
The Transport Layer takes responsibility for issues of reliability and flow control. It splits information into packets and reassembles remotely transmitted packets.

